WEBVTT

00:20.979 --> 00:22.981
[cryptic music]

00:27.902 --> 00:32.615
[Hatter] "You must be the change
you wish to see in the world."

00:33.742 --> 00:35.243
That's what Gandhi said.

00:37.662 --> 00:38.663
I…

00:40.415 --> 00:42.792
will create a utopian society.

00:45.420 --> 00:48.173
For all of those
who have fallen into despair,

00:51.843 --> 00:53.344
if we do not have hope,

00:53.887 --> 00:55.513
then we must create it!

00:59.267 --> 01:01.186
This will be the land of hope.

01:02.729 --> 01:03.730
SEASIDE PARADISE
TOKYO

01:03.813 --> 01:07.776
I will make this oasis
into the second Beach!

01:09.027 --> 01:11.029
[cryptic music crescendos]

01:25.668 --> 01:26.503
[clicks]

01:28.379 --> 01:30.381
[cryptic music climaxes]

01:36.930 --> 01:38.932
[theme music]

02:35.530 --> 02:37.532
[upbeat electronic music playing]

02:37.615 --> 02:39.450
BEACH

02:52.130 --> 02:53.339
[knocking on door]

03:01.055 --> 03:02.390
[knocking continues]

03:07.186 --> 03:08.354
[door opens]

03:09.105 --> 03:11.232
[approaching footsteps]

03:16.195 --> 03:17.947
How long are you gonna sleep?

03:18.990 --> 03:20.366
[Arisu groans]

03:21.451 --> 03:22.994
[Usagi] Are you hungover?

03:25.496 --> 03:27.498
[Arisu groans]

03:30.043 --> 03:32.503
[groaning continues]

03:32.587 --> 03:34.088
Did you get any information?

03:35.298 --> 03:36.716
I'm afraid not.

03:40.678 --> 03:43.014
I think I'd better get up
and get some info.

03:46.434 --> 03:48.603
[Usagi] Seems like Hatter
has taken a liking to you.

03:48.686 --> 03:49.687
[scoffs]

03:49.771 --> 03:53.066
You'd better be careful.
The militant corps will be watching you.

03:53.900 --> 03:56.277
And we have no idea
what they're capable of.

03:59.697 --> 04:01.699
["Good Times" by Jan Erik Nilsson playing]

04:03.451 --> 04:06.329
[Hiro] I was talking to these guys
who drove all the way to the suburbs.

04:06.412 --> 04:09.290
They were saying that
the further you get from the city,

04:09.374 --> 04:11.292
the crappier and more run-down
the streets are,

04:11.376 --> 04:13.962
and if you keep goin',
it looks like you're actually in a jungle.

04:14.462 --> 04:17.382
They decided they weren't taking
any chances and didn't go any further.

04:17.465 --> 04:18.299
Seriously?

04:18.383 --> 04:22.512
I heard that all the game arenas
are pretty much inside Tokyo!

04:22.595 --> 04:25.139
[DJ] Come on, people! Who wants to party?

04:25.223 --> 04:26.182
[all cheering]

04:27.100 --> 04:30.561
There are rumors about people
who tried escaping the country by boat,

04:30.645 --> 04:33.314
but then those lasers came down
from the sky and killed all of them.

04:33.398 --> 04:34.857
[chuckles]
You hear about that?

04:34.941 --> 04:36.067
Hang on a second.

04:36.150 --> 04:41.155
Does that mean that the only people
who are disappearing are in Tokyo?

04:41.239 --> 04:43.408
So, wait.
If this is only happening in Tokyo,

04:43.491 --> 04:46.703
wouldn't the SDF have come to rescue us?
That makes sense, right?

04:46.786 --> 04:48.204
And the fact that they haven't come,

04:48.288 --> 04:50.415
does that mean
that everyone in Japan has disappeared?

04:50.498 --> 04:52.041
The US Army didn't come either.

04:52.125 --> 04:53.584
[scoffs]
This is so weird.

04:53.668 --> 04:56.170
Could it be
that the whole world disappeared?

04:56.254 --> 04:57.547
[laughing]

04:57.630 --> 05:00.633
I don't know, man.
I think aliens put chips into our brains

05:00.717 --> 05:02.093
and are playin' with us.

05:02.635 --> 05:04.762
I don't think anyone could escape
from this place.

05:04.846 --> 05:05.680
[chuckles]

05:05.763 --> 05:07.181
Gimme a swig.
[groans]

05:07.265 --> 05:08.099
[slurps]

05:08.182 --> 05:10.184
["Good Times" by Jan Erik Nilsson playing]

05:11.102 --> 05:13.271
[Usagi] The more I hear,
the more depressing it gets.

05:14.856 --> 05:15.982
Yeah, I know…

05:16.733 --> 05:19.152
Our only hope might be
with those playing cards.

05:19.235 --> 05:21.195
[indistinct background chatter]

05:28.411 --> 05:31.456
All right.
I'll head over to the annex now.

05:33.249 --> 05:34.500
Just be careful, okay?

05:35.251 --> 05:37.503
I'll also get food supplies and weapons.

05:37.587 --> 05:40.131
And it'll be great
if I could get a little more information.

05:46.304 --> 05:48.264
Yeah, wouldn't that be real nice?

05:51.267 --> 05:53.311
[inaudible chatter]

05:55.396 --> 05:57.857
Hey! You guys mind if I ask you something?

06:01.110 --> 06:02.904
Wait, I'm not trying to hit on ya!

06:03.946 --> 06:05.531
[gunshots in distance]

06:18.586 --> 06:20.588
[clattering in distance]

06:32.058 --> 06:34.060
[ominous music]

06:44.570 --> 06:46.531
[ominous music builds]

06:54.622 --> 06:55.540
[Arisu groans]

07:01.546 --> 07:03.047
[cover rustles]

07:05.716 --> 07:07.718
[thrilling music]

07:09.595 --> 07:10.847
[coughs]

07:13.141 --> 07:15.560
[Chishiya] That's what
this utopia really looks like.

07:19.355 --> 07:20.940
Another Beach rule.

07:21.524 --> 07:23.401
"Death if you're a traitor."

07:24.694 --> 07:26.696
[terrifying music crescendos]

07:38.749 --> 07:39.625
[Chishiya] Arisu.

07:41.127 --> 07:44.505
You and Usagi seem to have gathered
a whole bunch of information.

07:45.381 --> 07:46.716
Are you two planning something?

07:49.427 --> 07:50.553
No, not really.

07:54.974 --> 07:56.767
[Chishiya] All right,
I'll cut to the chase.

07:58.186 --> 08:00.980
How do you think you're going to live
in a world full of despair?

08:02.398 --> 08:03.649
What?

08:15.328 --> 08:17.497
Look, all I want is some answers.

08:19.332 --> 08:21.459
Who's behind these sick games and…

08:23.794 --> 08:26.422
who killed my friends, Karube and Chota.

08:29.675 --> 08:31.677
[somber music]

08:32.178 --> 08:33.930
I thought I'd be able to survive

08:34.639 --> 08:37.266
and go back to the world
the way it used to be.

08:40.186 --> 08:41.854
But if that's not possible,

08:43.022 --> 08:45.566
I want Usagi to return at the very least.

08:47.610 --> 08:49.529
She's the only reason I'm alive.

08:52.990 --> 08:54.283
Very touching.

08:57.954 --> 08:59.121
This wish of yours…

09:00.456 --> 09:01.832
sure is nice,

09:04.210 --> 09:06.128
but not very practical, I'll tell you.

09:06.837 --> 09:07.797
[scoffs]

09:08.589 --> 09:13.594
You'd have to win every single game
coming up and become the next Number 1.

09:14.220 --> 09:15.304
Impossible.

09:15.388 --> 09:16.347
[Arisu sighs]

09:16.430 --> 09:18.224
Look, it's not about you guys, all right?

09:18.766 --> 09:20.768
We think you both have potential.

09:22.520 --> 09:25.481
- What?
- Yeah, that's why we're here right now.

09:27.608 --> 09:28.776
What do you mean?

09:31.028 --> 09:34.198
What would you say if I told you,
things could play out differently?

09:38.160 --> 09:39.412
[engine revving]

09:39.495 --> 09:41.205
[people cheering]

09:41.289 --> 09:43.541
[overlapping screaming]

09:43.624 --> 09:45.585
[Hatter] Let's go!

09:45.668 --> 09:47.420
[cheering]

09:49.880 --> 09:51.966
[Usagi] They've got a lot of guns.

09:52.633 --> 09:56.304
Their arsenal is in the deepest room
in the annex, and they have patrols too.

09:57.722 --> 09:59.682
As long as they have all those weapons,

09:59.765 --> 10:02.143
Hatter will be in control of everything.

10:02.935 --> 10:04.103
[sighs]

10:08.608 --> 10:09.650
[Usagi] What's the matter?

10:17.992 --> 10:19.160
[Hatter] I'm off!

10:19.243 --> 10:21.287
[people cheering]

10:24.123 --> 10:27.418
[Chishiya] Hatter's making sure
he keeps control of the militant corps,

10:28.127 --> 10:30.838
but it's only a matter of time
before they retaliate.

10:32.798 --> 10:34.634
And if that happens,

10:35.301 --> 10:38.846
this place will be run
by a bunch of brainless idiots with guns.

10:38.929 --> 10:40.806
Then it's cut and run.

10:42.183 --> 10:43.726
What are you planning?

10:46.812 --> 10:48.898
I'm planning
to steal all the playing cards…

10:50.691 --> 10:52.485
bail off the Beach.

10:52.568 --> 10:54.570
[suspenseful music]

10:55.780 --> 10:58.616
[people cheering]

10:58.699 --> 11:01.285
[upbeat action music]

11:02.870 --> 11:04.205
[Arisu] Beach.

11:05.706 --> 11:08.459
A pseudo-utopia
built on one guy's charisma.

11:11.587 --> 11:12.421
But then again,

11:13.756 --> 11:16.425
maybe we're the only ones
who think that way.

11:16.509 --> 11:17.927
BEACH

11:19.470 --> 11:21.263
There is no utopia in this world.

11:23.349 --> 11:24.392
Usagi.

11:26.811 --> 11:28.062
We need to talk.

11:30.606 --> 11:32.900
[foreboding music]

11:35.403 --> 11:38.656
KABUKICHO

11:38.739 --> 11:40.074
THIS WAY TO THE GAME ARENA

11:40.157 --> 11:42.118
[car engine rumbles]

11:47.581 --> 11:48.749
[engine stops]

11:49.959 --> 11:50.876
[feet stomp]

11:54.547 --> 11:55.714
[car door shuts]

11:55.798 --> 11:56.757
[man 1] This way.

12:02.388 --> 12:03.848
[Hatter] Kabuki District, huh?

12:05.766 --> 12:06.934
This takes me back.

12:08.060 --> 12:10.062
[eerie music]

12:19.738 --> 12:23.242
BEACH

12:23.325 --> 12:24.743
- I can't wait…
- [Tatta] Watch it!

12:24.827 --> 12:26.454
- Hey!
- Excuse me, sorry!

12:26.537 --> 12:28.497
- [panting]
- [footsteps echoing]

12:40.801 --> 12:43.721
Where the hell is that damn GPS chip?

12:44.805 --> 12:46.807
[Tatta panting]

12:48.392 --> 12:50.561
Okay, so this is where you are!
[exhales]

12:50.644 --> 12:52.146
[Ann] Did I say you could come in here?

12:54.523 --> 12:56.942
[muffled gasp]
Right.

12:57.026 --> 13:00.654
Something bad has happened.
Ju-- Just come with me, please!

13:01.238 --> 13:02.156
Hurry!

13:02.740 --> 13:04.241
[clattering]

13:08.913 --> 13:10.915
[man 2] Whoa, what are you doin' here?

13:10.998 --> 13:12.625
[Niragi] What the hell do you two want?

13:13.125 --> 13:14.793
No one asked you to come here!

13:15.961 --> 13:18.255
Actually, I'm the one who asked him.

13:20.341 --> 13:22.676
Yeah? Who says you can summon people now?

13:23.677 --> 13:26.013
There's something important
he has to hear.

13:27.681 --> 13:28.516
Let's go in.

13:31.268 --> 13:32.353
See you later.

13:39.318 --> 13:40.569
What's going on?

13:41.278 --> 13:45.074
Not a clue, but it's gotta be
something pretty serious.

13:49.620 --> 13:51.622
[ominous music]

14:09.431 --> 14:11.433
[ominous music climaxes]

14:19.483 --> 14:22.111
[somber music]

14:27.408 --> 14:28.450
[sighs]

14:28.534 --> 14:30.411
Apparently, he couldn't clear the game.

14:31.203 --> 14:33.747
The maintenance team
just happened to find him in Shinjuku

14:33.831 --> 14:35.958
while we were filling up with gas.

14:39.753 --> 14:42.464
[Niragi] Hey, do me a favor
and keep your hands off him.

14:42.548 --> 14:44.133
You're obsessed with dissecting things.

14:49.179 --> 14:50.723
[Ann] This is from a bullet.

14:51.307 --> 14:54.018
Did the game he was playing involve guns?

14:54.643 --> 14:56.020
Seems like it.

14:56.103 --> 14:58.772
Apparently, people around the game area
heard gunshots.

14:59.356 --> 15:00.691
[Niragi] Holy shit!

15:00.774 --> 15:03.611
Looks like he should've brought
the militant corps along with him.

15:07.489 --> 15:09.825
[tense music]

15:14.788 --> 15:17.583
So now what? What happens to the Beach?

15:19.168 --> 15:21.253
[Mira] Nobody says a word about this,
understood?

15:21.962 --> 15:23.505
We don't want people freaking out.

15:25.716 --> 15:28.052
I'll step in as leader since I'm Number 2.

15:28.636 --> 15:30.012
[Niragi] Wait a second.

15:31.597 --> 15:34.475
Shouldn't the strongest person
be the leader?

15:35.768 --> 15:36.727
In case you didn't know,

15:36.810 --> 15:39.438
we're the ones who have been
getting rid of the traitors,

15:40.105 --> 15:42.816
but we've been thrown into the shadows
the whole time.

15:42.900 --> 15:44.818
This bullshit ends now, you got that?

15:44.902 --> 15:46.779
If Number 1 dies,

15:46.862 --> 15:49.740
everyone moves up by a number.
We all knew that.

15:49.823 --> 15:52.660
Yeah, well, this elitist dictator is dead.

15:53.369 --> 15:55.079
The power has shifted, hasn't it?

15:56.205 --> 15:59.375
Let's just be democratic
and go with the majority.

16:00.584 --> 16:01.835
[scoffs]

16:01.919 --> 16:05.381
Who's with me and thinks
that Aguni should be our new leader?

16:06.090 --> 16:08.092
[tense music]

16:14.890 --> 16:17.935
[scoffs]
Are you all serious right now?

16:19.436 --> 16:20.437
Last Boss.

16:21.105 --> 16:23.190
[tense music crescendos]

16:26.694 --> 16:27.569
[blade scrapes]

16:32.449 --> 16:34.451
[tense music climaxes]

16:38.163 --> 16:39.790
So I'll ask again.

16:40.499 --> 16:42.710
Who thinks Aguni should be leader?

16:46.588 --> 16:48.007
[snorts]

16:51.802 --> 16:53.804
[suspenseful music]

16:56.640 --> 16:57.558
[Mira] This…

16:58.142 --> 17:00.019
- is not a democracy.
- [scoffs]

17:01.061 --> 17:03.439
But I think it is, isn't it?

17:03.522 --> 17:04.356
[gun clatters]

17:05.190 --> 17:07.359
You can vote however you want, right?

17:10.279 --> 17:12.281
[suspenseful music builds]

17:17.411 --> 17:19.663
And how about
the former Number 2 over there?

17:21.123 --> 17:22.166
What do you think?

17:28.172 --> 17:29.131
[Niragi chuckles]

17:32.926 --> 17:34.636
- [cocks gun]
- And what about you?

17:36.096 --> 17:38.098
[suspenseful music builds]

17:40.893 --> 17:44.688
Chishiya,
you're not looking down on us, are ya?

17:45.314 --> 17:46.774
Y'all morons in the corps?

17:48.692 --> 17:49.568
[gun clatters]

17:50.569 --> 17:53.197
Those eyes of yours piss me off sometimes,
you know that?

17:54.281 --> 17:56.867
You really think you're better than us,
don't ya?

17:56.950 --> 17:58.952
[suspenseful music builds]

18:02.831 --> 18:05.042
I vote for Aguni to be the leader.

18:06.710 --> 18:09.296
I'm pretty sure
that's what you want to hear, don't you?

18:11.840 --> 18:12.758
[scoffs]

18:12.841 --> 18:16.136
Well, let this be a reminder
of how you should act in the future.

18:18.388 --> 18:21.225
Hey, why are you looking so freaked out?

18:22.559 --> 18:25.270
I thought I told you
to give me an answer there?

18:26.313 --> 18:28.190
Whose side are you on, anyway?

18:28.941 --> 18:30.192
[swooshing]

18:30.734 --> 18:33.362
[giggles]
Just about to shit your pants there, huh?

18:33.445 --> 18:36.031
[Niragi laughs]
Look at his face!

18:38.075 --> 18:39.576
All right.

18:40.452 --> 18:42.663
Looks like we have a unanimous decision.

18:42.746 --> 18:45.290
So, we've got a new leader, right?

18:45.374 --> 18:47.459
Hatter would not allow this.

18:48.752 --> 18:51.171
If he were alive,
he would not have allowed this.

18:51.255 --> 18:52.589
[Niragi chuckles]

18:53.799 --> 18:55.717
But he's not alive, is he?

18:55.801 --> 18:56.969
[bangs]

18:58.679 --> 19:01.807
The dead really have no say
as to what's going on. Watch.

19:01.890 --> 19:04.852
[banging]

19:04.935 --> 19:06.061
See?

19:06.687 --> 19:08.188
- See?
- [banging continues]

19:09.690 --> 19:10.566
[spits]

19:10.649 --> 19:11.775
[Aguni] That's enough.

19:18.699 --> 19:20.159
From this day onwards,

19:21.577 --> 19:23.287
I will be the Beach's new king.

19:25.664 --> 19:28.125
[sighs]
Yeah, let's hear it for the King, huh?

19:28.208 --> 19:31.670
[applauding]

19:33.797 --> 19:37.301
Okay, boss.
Time for the succession ceremony, right?

19:37.384 --> 19:40.304
Maybe you should open up
the black envelope.

19:40.387 --> 19:43.640
[tense music]

19:50.814 --> 19:52.357
[Chishiya] The black envelope.

19:53.775 --> 19:57.112
All the playing cards collected
by members of the Beach

19:57.905 --> 20:00.657
are kept in the safe
in Hatter's royal suite.

20:02.034 --> 20:04.578
The code for opening the safe

20:05.287 --> 20:08.707
is sealed inside the black envelope.

20:11.251 --> 20:14.046
The envelope is kept in a secret location.

20:16.465 --> 20:20.802
And the only time it's opened
is when there's a new Number 1.

20:22.137 --> 20:23.722
[rustling]

20:25.766 --> 20:29.353
The new Number 1 opens the envelope
in front of the executives,

20:29.937 --> 20:32.481
but only he sees the code to the safe.

20:33.982 --> 20:35.984
[paper rustles]

20:36.610 --> 20:39.404
[tranquil music]

20:42.616 --> 20:45.786
Then, he places the paper
with the code written on it

20:45.869 --> 20:48.705
into a new envelope and seals it again.

20:49.456 --> 20:52.584
It then must be signed
by all the executives.

20:52.668 --> 20:53.627
[stamp thuds]

20:54.211 --> 20:56.213
[pensive music]

21:03.262 --> 21:05.889
First, Arisu will infiltrate
the royal suite.

21:06.556 --> 21:08.267
Then he'll search for the safe,

21:08.350 --> 21:10.644
and steal all the playing cards inside.

21:12.396 --> 21:15.399
- And how do I get the code?
- Don't worry about that.

21:16.650 --> 21:19.111
I'll let you know
when you're in front of the safe.

21:21.947 --> 21:23.407
I sure hope you're right.

21:24.408 --> 21:25.575
I'm on it.

21:26.159 --> 21:27.160
[radio clatters]

21:27.244 --> 21:29.746
Usagi and Kuina will be on the lookout.

21:30.789 --> 21:34.334
This is too dangerous.
They'll kill us if they see us.

21:39.381 --> 21:41.800
I don't think we have any other choice.

21:43.552 --> 21:47.556
Now that Hatter's dead,
the unity in the Beach is wavering.

21:47.639 --> 21:49.349
I think this plan could work for us.

21:50.892 --> 21:52.894
[suspenseful music]

21:56.940 --> 21:58.775
[breathes heavily]

22:03.864 --> 22:05.907
I'm here to tell you,
we have a new leader.

22:05.991 --> 22:07.826
[people murmuring]

22:07.909 --> 22:08.785
[woman] What happened?

22:08.869 --> 22:10.746
[Niragi] Hatter is no longer with us,

22:11.330 --> 22:13.623
and that leader has been chosen.

22:14.207 --> 22:15.625
The new leader is Aguni.

22:16.209 --> 22:18.211
[people murmuring]

22:19.838 --> 22:21.298
[Niragi] Everybody, shut up!

22:23.633 --> 22:28.055
It seems as though Hatter failed
in his game. He just couldn't crack it.

22:29.097 --> 22:32.267
A vote was taken,
and the executive was unanimous,

22:32.809 --> 22:35.395
and Aguni was voted as our new Number 1.

22:37.898 --> 22:40.609
Now, let's hear from Aguni.

22:41.485 --> 22:44.196
You better all listen carefully.

22:52.746 --> 22:53.914
[Aguni] Niragi

22:53.997 --> 22:56.416
said everything that needs to be said.

22:58.085 --> 23:00.545
All right, the new leader
is making a speech in the lobby.

23:02.798 --> 23:05.801
[Chishiya] All members of the executive
and the militant corps

23:05.884 --> 23:07.260
are here at the annex.

23:08.261 --> 23:10.347
We're not gonna get
another chance like this.

23:11.181 --> 23:13.600
[tense action music]

23:13.683 --> 23:16.394
I'll let you guys know
if there are any changes here.

23:16.478 --> 23:18.522
- I'm counting on you, Arisu.
- [radio buzzes off]

23:20.941 --> 23:21.942
Copy that.

23:27.072 --> 23:29.950
[Aguni] Now that Hatter is gone
and I'm the Number 1,

23:30.617 --> 23:33.370
I have full control over the Beach.

23:33.870 --> 23:37.082
Follow my orders.
I want you to live for me,

23:38.500 --> 23:40.544
and you may have to die for me.

23:40.627 --> 23:41.711
[snorts]

23:46.007 --> 23:47.008
[sighs]

23:50.137 --> 23:51.054
[door knob clanks]

23:51.138 --> 23:52.430
[exhales]

23:54.933 --> 23:56.017
[whispers] I found it.

23:57.561 --> 23:59.104
All right, what's the code?

23:59.187 --> 24:00.814
8-0-2-2.

24:01.314 --> 24:03.233
So you saw what's in the letter?

24:03.775 --> 24:04.818
[Chishiya] No.

24:05.443 --> 24:08.029
But Aguni's expression
pretty much said it all.

24:09.322 --> 24:10.657
[Chishiya] When he opened it,

24:11.158 --> 24:13.243
his face kinda went all dark,

24:14.536 --> 24:16.496
like he was completely surprised

24:17.247 --> 24:19.291
and really perplexed.

24:21.501 --> 24:23.628
I'm pretty sure
there was nothing written on it.

24:24.462 --> 24:26.715
Nothing? Then how did you get the code?

24:26.798 --> 24:27.757
[giggles]

24:29.092 --> 24:30.760
From the wax seal.

24:31.928 --> 24:35.348
The Boss seals it with his ring.
It has numbers on it.

24:36.808 --> 24:38.602
And that's the code.

24:39.477 --> 24:40.979
8-0-2-2.

24:44.482 --> 24:46.610
Sure as hell
wouldn't want to be your enemy.

24:49.154 --> 24:53.408
[keypad beeping]

24:54.951 --> 24:56.953
[alarm beeping rapidly]

24:57.037 --> 24:58.788
[Arisu] It's not opening!

25:00.123 --> 25:01.082
[safe clanking]

25:01.166 --> 25:02.375
Chishiya!

25:04.085 --> 25:05.629
Chishiya, you there?

25:05.712 --> 25:08.256
[beeping continues]

25:08.340 --> 25:11.301
Yeah, I gotta hand it to you.
You really got balls.

25:18.975 --> 25:21.269
- Why would you…
- [Usagi] Let me go!

25:21.770 --> 25:24.648
- Relax, calm down!
- Usagi!

25:24.731 --> 25:25.565
[whacks]

25:25.649 --> 25:26.733
[Usagi shouts]
Arisu!

25:26.816 --> 25:29.945
Stop crying for your boyfriend,
you stupid bitch!

25:30.028 --> 25:31.279
- [Arisu grunts]
- [Usagi] Arisu!

25:31.363 --> 25:32.447
[screams]

25:32.530 --> 25:33.490
[thuds]

25:34.199 --> 25:35.283
[Niragi laughs]

25:35.367 --> 25:37.869
- Chishiya, I owe you.
- [Niragi grunts]

25:37.953 --> 25:39.871
We wouldn't have caught them
if it wasn't for you.

25:39.955 --> 25:41.456
- [Usagi] Let go… Arisu!
- Yeah, well…

25:41.539 --> 25:42.707
Just wanna be of service.

25:42.791 --> 25:44.125
- [Niragi grunts]
- [Arisu groaning]

25:44.209 --> 25:46.544
[Usagi] Stop it! Stop it!

25:46.628 --> 25:47.629
[Niragi cackles]

25:49.172 --> 25:51.341
[Arisu groaning]

25:54.010 --> 25:55.971
[winces, cries]

25:56.054 --> 25:57.597
[Usagi wails]
Arisu!

25:58.223 --> 26:00.433
Well, now. Looks like…

26:01.977 --> 26:03.812
Someone's gone night-night.

26:06.690 --> 26:07.524
[exhales]

26:08.608 --> 26:10.902
All right. Bring him to the room.

26:18.118 --> 26:20.036
[Arisu breathing heavily]

26:28.837 --> 26:32.632
[Niragi] Well, rumor has it
that your visa expires tomorrow.

26:36.219 --> 26:41.141
Without your sense of hearing
or your sight, you're like a sitting duck.

26:41.725 --> 26:44.936
I can just imagine the terror
you're feeling as you sit here

26:45.020 --> 26:47.439
and wait for the laser
to burn through your skull!

26:47.522 --> 26:49.441
- [Niragi chuckles]
- [Arisu grunts]

26:49.524 --> 26:52.110
[Niragi] But for now…
[exhales]

26:52.193 --> 26:56.406
…I'll just enjoy all this precious time
I'm gonna have with your girlfriend.

26:56.489 --> 26:57.365
[exhales cheekily]

26:57.449 --> 26:58.825
[muffled scream]

26:58.908 --> 27:01.202
- [men laugh]
- [Niragi] See ya!

27:03.913 --> 27:08.376
- [Arisu's muffled screaming]
- [men laughing]

27:10.420 --> 27:12.005
[feet thumping]

27:12.881 --> 27:14.549
[door slams, lock clicks]

27:14.632 --> 27:16.426
[screaming continues]

27:18.261 --> 27:19.554
[muffled straining]

27:19.637 --> 27:21.639
[suspenseful music]

27:41.493 --> 27:43.495
[suspenseful music continues]

28:01.513 --> 28:03.765
[Chishiya]
How are things going over there, Kuina?

28:05.517 --> 28:08.645
All right, I guess.
Aguni is still in his room.

28:10.313 --> 28:12.565
[groans]
I'm dying of boredom over here.

28:13.900 --> 28:16.945
[Chishiya]
Well, let's go ahead with our plan, then.

28:19.364 --> 28:22.033
I have no idea
if Arisu is smart or stupid.

28:22.659 --> 28:25.412
There's no way
they'd keep the cards in an ordinary safe.

28:26.955 --> 28:29.541
[Kuina] Then where do you think
the real safe is?

28:30.917 --> 28:33.545
I'm not sure,
but when Arisu found the fake safe,

28:34.337 --> 28:36.881
Aguni, who usually has a good poker face,

28:37.465 --> 28:39.634
was glancing towards something else.

28:42.971 --> 28:46.307
I think that whatever's in that envelope

28:46.891 --> 28:50.103
isn't a code or some blank letter.

28:53.398 --> 28:55.942
I think it might just be a drawing.

29:05.201 --> 29:06.828
[approaching footsteps]

29:09.998 --> 29:10.832
[sighs]

29:13.877 --> 29:15.879
[tense music]

29:17.172 --> 29:18.173
[painting clatters]

29:19.883 --> 29:20.759
[Chishiya] Found it.

29:21.551 --> 29:23.386
[Kuina] So this is
why you sacrificed them?

29:25.221 --> 29:28.808
Yeah, well, you gotta give something
to get something.

29:29.976 --> 29:32.979
They were pawns, that's all. Shit happens.

29:33.062 --> 29:36.483
[sighs]
Yeah, well, all I know…

29:37.525 --> 29:40.862
is that I sure as hell
wouldn't want to be your enemy.

29:40.945 --> 29:42.030
[soft chuckle]

29:42.113 --> 29:43.615
Yeah, I get that a lot.

29:45.909 --> 29:46.910
[gasps]

29:51.331 --> 29:53.249
[security system beeping]

29:53.333 --> 29:54.459
[safe door pops]

29:54.542 --> 29:56.544
[tense music]

30:26.741 --> 30:28.743
[suspenseful music]

30:28.827 --> 30:30.161
[Kuina exhales in relief]

30:40.797 --> 30:42.799
[box clicks]

30:44.509 --> 30:45.468
[door slams]

30:48.304 --> 30:50.348
- [Usagi] Get your hands off me!
- Shut up!

30:50.431 --> 30:52.517
- Hurry…
- Stop struggling, man!

30:52.600 --> 30:53.601
[both] And, heave!

30:53.685 --> 30:54.602
[man 3] Now relax.

30:54.686 --> 30:56.938
[men grunting]

30:57.522 --> 30:59.357
- [man 4] Stop resisting.
- [Usagi] Get off me!

30:59.440 --> 31:00.817
[men grunting, pounding]

31:00.900 --> 31:03.361
- [whistling]
- [Usagi grunting]

31:05.697 --> 31:07.574
- [thuds]
- [Usagi continues grunting]

31:07.657 --> 31:08.616
[scoffs]

31:12.537 --> 31:14.247
[panting]

31:17.750 --> 31:19.752
[breathing heavily]

31:19.836 --> 31:21.713
[zipper rattling]

31:22.714 --> 31:24.716
[sinister music]

31:25.800 --> 31:27.760
[breathing heavily]

31:28.928 --> 31:35.393
Rape, assault, fraud, arson, and murder.

31:36.644 --> 31:39.314
Why do you think
these things are all against the law?

31:41.983 --> 31:44.360
[Usagi grunting]

31:46.195 --> 31:49.032
You tell me, why do you think
they're all against the law?

31:50.909 --> 31:52.702
- [Usagi breathing heavily]
- [Niragi chuckles]

31:54.287 --> 31:56.289
Because they're all in our nature.

31:57.832 --> 32:00.084
[breathing heavily]

32:00.168 --> 32:03.755
Left to their own devices, humans will
rape, steal, and kill each other.

32:03.838 --> 32:05.965
[Usagi breathing nervously]

32:07.258 --> 32:09.010
Because that's what we're all about.

32:12.889 --> 32:15.308
[breathing heavily]

32:20.521 --> 32:23.066
But there are no laws here, are there?

32:24.233 --> 32:27.070
It's a waste to deny our basic instincts,
don't you think?

32:27.153 --> 32:29.447
[panting]
I mean, it's inside us all.

32:30.114 --> 32:32.450
It even empowers us, doesn't it?

32:32.533 --> 32:33.618
[Usagi grunts]

32:33.701 --> 32:35.787
[Niragi cackles]

32:42.001 --> 32:43.795
[Usagi breathing heavily]

32:46.214 --> 32:47.048
[Usagi exclaims]

32:47.131 --> 32:48.091
[snaps]

32:48.174 --> 32:49.300
[Niragi screams]

32:50.134 --> 32:51.678
[growls in pain]

32:51.761 --> 32:53.763
[tense music]

32:54.722 --> 32:55.848
[inhales deeply]

32:56.516 --> 32:57.725
[grunts]

32:57.809 --> 32:59.143
[panting]

32:59.727 --> 33:01.229
[grunts]

33:01.312 --> 33:02.647
[Niragi] Don't fuck with me.

33:03.523 --> 33:05.900
[Usagi breathing heavily]

33:06.609 --> 33:08.361
The fun is just starting.

33:11.072 --> 33:13.282
[power winding down]

33:15.076 --> 33:17.078
- [light flicking]
- [power winding up]

33:17.161 --> 33:18.246
[Niragi gasps]

33:24.168 --> 33:25.253
[gasps]

33:32.802 --> 33:34.846
Well, I guess
I can get rid of this now, too.

33:36.097 --> 33:40.560
Don't you feel sorry for him?
Arisu, I mean.

33:41.394 --> 33:42.687
Sorry for him?

33:43.813 --> 33:46.566
Hmm. Yeah, I know I do.

33:47.275 --> 33:48.484
[sighs]

33:51.529 --> 33:54.198
Sometimes we have to do things
in order to survive.

34:00.246 --> 34:03.666
If you're so worried about him,
then you should help him.

34:15.053 --> 34:16.095
No way…

34:19.015 --> 34:20.141
W-- Wait!

34:25.438 --> 34:26.939
[laser zaps]

34:27.023 --> 34:28.733
[crackling]

34:28.816 --> 34:31.444
[ominous music]

34:33.946 --> 34:35.948
[lasers buzzing]

34:38.993 --> 34:40.036
Seriously?

34:40.536 --> 34:42.538
[ominous music builds]

34:46.084 --> 34:48.086
[lasers buzzing]

34:49.378 --> 34:51.380
[ominous music builds]

34:54.092 --> 34:57.804
[muffled wailing]

35:00.306 --> 35:02.308
[PA chiming]

35:04.018 --> 35:06.104
[male announcer]
We would like to take this opportunity

35:06.187 --> 35:10.483
to sincerely thank you for staying
at Seaside Paradise, Tokyo.

35:10.566 --> 35:13.194
As a token of our appreciation,

35:13.277 --> 35:18.449
we will now commence a game
with all 58 participants in the venue.

35:18.533 --> 35:20.076
1 PER PERSON

35:21.911 --> 35:24.539
THE GAME WILL NOW COMMENCE

35:24.622 --> 35:26.624
[suspenseful music]

35:29.710 --> 35:30.837
The Beach is…

35:31.838 --> 35:33.131
a game arena?

35:33.714 --> 35:35.550
[female announcer] Difficulty,

35:35.633 --> 35:36.968
Ten of Hearts.

35:37.051 --> 35:38.010
GAME DIFFICULTY

35:39.762 --> 35:43.224
- "Ten of Hearts"!
- It happened at last.

35:43.933 --> 35:45.226
[grunts]

35:46.519 --> 35:50.606
[female announcer] All participants
must assemble in the lobby immediately.

35:50.690 --> 35:53.985
The rules of the game
will then be explained.

35:55.987 --> 35:59.657
I repeat. All participants must assemble

35:59.740 --> 36:01.909
- in the lobby immediately.
- [straining]

36:02.660 --> 36:04.787
[muffled whining]

36:04.871 --> 36:07.415
[people clamoring]

36:17.717 --> 36:19.719
[panting]

36:24.056 --> 36:26.017
[man 5] Hey, there's a game
starting in the lobby!

36:26.100 --> 36:27.685
- [woman 1] Let's go!
- [woman 2] Hurry!

36:27.768 --> 36:29.937
- [woman 3] Quick!
- [man 6] Anyone know what game it is?

36:30.021 --> 36:31.522
[man 5] It's Ten of Hearts!

36:31.606 --> 36:34.025
Hurry up! Hurry, hurry. Come on!

36:34.108 --> 36:35.109
[woman 3] Move it!

36:35.193 --> 36:36.986
- [PA chiming]
- [people murmuring]

36:48.039 --> 36:50.041
[suspenseful action music]

37:04.347 --> 37:06.307
[Usagi grunts]

37:10.019 --> 37:12.021
[music fades out]

37:13.272 --> 37:15.274
[people murmuring]

37:15.942 --> 37:17.026
Momoka!

37:18.402 --> 37:20.947
Momoka! Why…

37:21.030 --> 37:22.490
[sobs]

37:22.573 --> 37:24.951
[soft tense music]

37:26.786 --> 37:27.828
[phones chiming]

37:27.912 --> 37:30.665
[female announcer] Game, "Witch Hunt".

37:30.748 --> 37:32.083
[people clamoring]

37:32.166 --> 37:34.835
[female announcer]
The murderous witch who killed this girl

37:34.919 --> 37:37.255
is hiding amongst you in plain sight.

37:39.048 --> 37:42.218
The witch role is not limited to women.

37:42.301 --> 37:43.344
[people murmuring]

37:43.427 --> 37:44.553
She's hiding here?

37:44.637 --> 37:47.348
[female announcer] To clear the game,
you must find the witch

37:47.431 --> 37:50.434
and burn him or her
in the Fire of Judgment.

37:51.102 --> 37:53.562
Time limit, two hours.

37:53.646 --> 37:55.815
[tense music]

37:55.898 --> 37:58.359
[fire crackling]

37:58.442 --> 38:02.488
[muffled screaming]

38:04.532 --> 38:07.368
[tense music builds]

38:17.044 --> 38:19.046
[flames crackling]

38:25.886 --> 38:27.763
TIME LIMIT

38:35.354 --> 38:37.398
[closing theme music]

40:20.376 --> 40:22.378
[music fades out]
